-- a table dropped without SYNC keeps the root until the drop finishes
It is dropped and keeps its data until the drop finishes, retry after that (`DROP TABLE ... SYNC` waits for the drop). (BAD_ARGUMENTS)
-- a table detached without SYNC keeps the root while its detached instance is alive
It is detached and its detached instance is still alive, retry after it is released (in an `Atomic` database `DETACH TABLE ... SYNC` waits for that). (BAD_ARGUMENTS)
